claim=dict(id='C-read-context',kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='When the leader releases an admitted forwarded ReadIndex request after quorum confirmation, the ReadIndexResp sent to its requester must carry that released request\'s SystemCtx unchanged, so the requester can associate ReadyToRead with the same operation. Coalesced confirmation may raise the read index but must not replace an earlier request\'s context with another request\'s context.',source_ids=['S-read-identity-contract','S-read-contract','S-read-aggregation','S-read-response','S-forward-read','S-read-consumer'],scope=dict(description='Per-operation response correlation for released forwarded requests within a stable leader term and membership after a current-term entry is committed.',assumptions=['Distinct nonzero SystemCtx values identify independently admitted requests.','Requests and quorum acknowledgements originate from the actual Peer handlers in one controlled history.','Non-Byzantine members; a delayed earlier response may overlap later traffic; no crash or membership change during the selected history.'],excluded=['No requirement that unconfirmed or dropped requests succeed.','No deadline or infinite-stall claim; no end-to-end NodeHost completion or stale-read consequence.','No backend crash atomicity or snapshot-recovery property.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=['S-read-aggregation','S-read-response','S-forward-read','S-read-consumer'],expectation_ids=['S-read-identity-contract','S-read-contract'],binding_ids=['BD-read-emit','BD-read-receive'],derivation='SystemCtx is explicitly the identity of a ReadIndex operation, and ReadyToRead identifies a prior batch. The async ReadIndex API returns a per-operation RequestState. Leader confirm retains each pending record and releases a prefix; follower receipt copies the response context into ReadyToRead, whose consumer performs an exact-key batch lookup. Therefore a response for a released record must preserve its stored identity. This is an identity-preservation duty at release, not a promise of success for all calls. The suspected implementation difference is not treated as a conflicting normative source.',applicability='Forwarded requests that are actually released by a quorum confirmation in the same authority epoch.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['No obligation to immediately complete a still-pending request.','One request or local-only prefix processing can preserve identity and does not exercise the remote-prefix discrepancy.']))
